      "page": 3,
      "text": "1. Implementation\n\nThe document has been created and approved by the General Assembly of 09.11.2024.\nThe document and its rules have been implemented since the 2025 season.\n\n2. Definition and Rules\n\nA Belt flag is an element hung on a belt designed to show your belt number in the list.\nA Belt flag must be made of fabric or leather.\nA Belt flag must conform with the “Textiles and Leather’ document.\n\nAs a competitor, it is required to wear a Belt flag with your belt number during buhurt fights.t is not required\nfor duel and outrance fights.\n\nA competitor may have a second Belt flag that is decorative. No more than two Belt flags may be worn by\na competitor.\n\n3. General Requirements\n\nBelts flags consist of a base and a number.\n\nBase must:\n● have a shape that can be square, rectangular or triangular,\n● have atrim to be worn with a belt,\n● be made of one main color.\n\nSome decoration can be added on the edges of the base.\nSuch decoration must not interfere with the readability of the Belt flag.\n\nNumbers must:\n● have individual figures from 0 to 9,\n● be from 01 to 99,\n● be written in Arabic numerals,\n● be 13cm tall as a minimum.\n\nNumbers can be of any color, contrasting with the base main color.\nAll Belt flags must respect the following dimensions:\n\n● Length: from 26 cm to 36 cm.\n● Width: from 14 cm to 18 cm.\n\n36! Flags v. 26.1 3/6",
